<title>USA: Frontier Airlines asks DOT for Laguardia slots.</title>
<headline>Frontier Airlines asks DOT for Laguardia slots.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Frontier Airlines Inc said Friday it has asked the U.S. Department of Transportation for an exemption to the &quot;slot&quot; restrictions limiting air service to New York's LaGuardia Airport.</p>
<p>If the waiver is granted, Frontier said it plans to schedule three daily nonstop flights in each direction between its Denver hub and LaGuardia.</p>
<p>Frontier said its proposed flights would provide the only competition to United Airlines monopoly service in the Denver-LaGuardia nonstop market.</p>
<p>Frontier operates a fleet of 10 Boeing 737s on routes linking Denver to 14 cities in 11 states.</p>
</text>
